course: dictionary
lesson: 6360
title: Mr, the polite title
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mr is short for «Mister». We put it in front of a man's family name, like «Mr Hughes has a cold.» It is a polite way to talk about or speak to a man.
explain: You can write Mr with a surname, like Mr Patel, or with a full name, like Mr John Brown. The word is always the same, but the name after it changes.
explain: At school you call a male teacher «Mr» plus his surname, such as Mr Jones. Keep using the title until an adult tells you that you can use their first name.
fact: Mr is short for «Mister».
fact: Mr goes before a man's surname or full name, such as «Mr Pryce» or «Mr John Brown».
fact: Other titles like Mrs, Miss, Ms and Mx also go before names, and each one is used for different people.
fact: In stories, names like «Mr Fox» and «Mr Men» use Mr to show a character is a man.
fact: Manners matter: use the title and surname until an adult says you can use their first name.
exercise: «Mr Hughes has a cold.» What does Mr stand for? | Miss | Madam | *Mister | Master
exercise: Which of these is a correct use of Mr? | Pryce Mr | Mr Greenhouse | Mr and | *Mr Pryce
exercise: Owen's football smashed «Mr Patel's greenhouse» in Leeds. Whose greenhouse was it? | Maddie's | The football's | *Mr Patel's | Owen's
test: In the fable, what did «Mr Crow» hold in his beak? | A letter | *A cheese | A football | A fox
test: Which title is used for a woman or girl? | Mr | *Miss | Pryce | Patel
exam: «Mr Brown still gives looks that could boil water.» What is Mr short for? | Madam | Mistress | *Mister | Master
